{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Nor shall you favor a poor man in his dispute.</b> The term <b>בְּרִיבוֹ</b> alludes, in the manner of our Sages of blessed memory (Leviticus Rabbah 34), to the idea that the poor man brings a dispute against his Maker — why does He sustain all yet leave him hungry and naked — and whoever gives a coin to a poor man and provides for him thereby silences the poor man's dispute from before the heavens. And at a time when there is no one showing grace to the poor, the poor man's plea is a plea that is heard and anguished. Therefore HaShem commands that one should not allow the poor man's dispute with his Maker to continue, but rather one should show him grace, in keeping with the One who shows grace to the poor."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:32:35.826878900Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}